---
description: Keep function definitions and parameters on a single line
alwaysApply: true
---

# Single-line function definitions

Always write function and method signatures on one line. Do not wrap parameters across multiple lines.

```python
# ❌ BAD
def create_item(
    name: str,
    quantity: int,
    storehome_id: int,
) -> Item:
    ...

# ✅ GOOD
def create_item(name: str, quantity: int, storehome_id: int) -> Item:
    ...
```

```javascript
# ❌ BAD
function searchLibrary(
  query,
  category,
) {
  ...
}

# ✅ GOOD
function searchLibrary(query, category) {
  ...
}
```

Same rule for `async def`, lambdas used as named functions, class methods, and JS/TS arrow functions assigned as functions.
